  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1409.08 Recordkeeping",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1409.08 Recordkeeping.\n\n(a) A used oil burner shall keep the following records:\n\n(1) For at least 3 years from the date of acceptance, a record of acceptance for each used oil shipment accepted for burning, in the form of a log, invoice, manifest, bill of lading, or other shipping document, that includes:\n\na. The name, address, and EPA identification number of the transporter that delivered the used oil to the used oil burner;\n\nb. The name, address, and if applicable, EPA identification number of the generator or processor/re-refiner from which the used oil was sent;\n\nc. The quantity of used oil accepted; and\n\nd. The date of acceptance;\n\n(2) Information gathered and records and results of used oil analyses performed, as applicable, to demonstrate compliance with Env-Hw 1409.03(d), for at least 3 years from the date the used oil burner last receives a shipment of specification used oil from that used oil handler; and\n\n(3) The certification required in Env-Hw 1409.07, for at least 3 years from the date the used oil burner last receives a shipment of off-specification used oil from that used oil handler.\n\n(b) The 3-year record retention period for the records specified in this section shall be extended automatically while any enforcement action is pending.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
